WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.136 --> 00:00:03.719
(happy Italian folk music)

00:00:13.523 --> 00:00:14.452
- Hi, I'm Hannah.

00:00:14.452 --> 00:00:16.112
Your friendly neighborhood wine mom

00:00:16.112 --> 00:00:17.737
and if you're anything
like me, you believe that

00:00:17.737 --> 00:00:20.448
a glass of wine at eight
p.m. makes you a better mom.

00:00:20.448 --> 00:00:22.756
So, pour yourself a glass and let's talk.

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:24.490
Tonight we're drinking red wine.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.185
This is what I like to call grown-up wine.

00:00:27.185 --> 00:00:29.927
And I always drink this wine
when I'm around other adults

00:00:29.927 --> 00:00:33.160
and trying to be an adult
and I'm like, (sniffs)

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.262
"Mmm, yes this is a great red,"

00:00:35.262 --> 00:00:37.764
but it's actually like kind
of strong and kind of intense.

00:00:37.764 --> 00:00:38.881
Like tonight's topic.

00:00:38.881 --> 00:00:40.823
Tonight we're gonna talk about

00:00:40.823 --> 00:00:43.403
the worst parts of childbirth.

00:00:43.403 --> 00:00:45.373
You thought pregnancy was bad.

00:00:45.373 --> 00:00:48.430
Strap yourselves in again
because this is a wild ride.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:53.225
There's pain, suffering,
beauty, disgustingness, fluids.

00:00:53.225 --> 00:00:55.551
I already anticipate the comments.

00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:58.203
"Oh you just made me
not want kids anymore!"

00:00:58.203 --> 00:01:01.429
And I don't care because
you deserve to know.

00:01:01.429 --> 00:01:03.262
So, let's get started.

00:01:05.174 --> 00:01:07.757
Ohh, hm, I don't like red wine.

00:01:09.053 --> 00:01:12.013
So just so you know, I had both
of my births in a hospital.

00:01:12.013 --> 00:01:14.963
So, what I'm gonna say
applies to my experiences.

00:01:14.963 --> 00:01:17.063
Yours might of been different,
but that's all good.

00:01:17.063 --> 00:01:18.118
So, let's go.

00:01:18.118 --> 00:01:20.192
Let's start with the worst part.

00:01:20.192 --> 00:01:21.025
Ready?

00:01:21.025 --> 00:01:23.758
It's not what you think it
would be, which is pushing

00:01:23.758 --> 00:01:24.594
out the child.

00:01:24.594 --> 00:01:27.857
It's actually this little
thing called contractions.

00:01:27.857 --> 00:01:30.512
It's like your body's way of saying,

00:01:30.512 --> 00:01:32.056
"Get this out of me".

00:01:32.056 --> 00:01:35.922
But instead of being like, "Oh
hey, excuse me could you like

00:01:35.922 --> 00:01:36.906
"start getting this out?"

00:01:36.906 --> 00:01:39.573
Your body's like, "Get this out!

00:01:41.209 --> 00:01:42.774
"Get it out of me!"

00:01:42.774 --> 00:01:45.454
The best way that I can describe it

00:01:45.454 --> 00:01:50.038
is like a chainsaw has
gone haywire inside of you

00:01:50.038 --> 00:01:51.982
and it's trying to get out.

00:01:51.982 --> 00:01:55.088
They get so bad, that you
will barf on yourself.

00:01:55.088 --> 00:01:58.575
I've literally barfed on
myself during a contraction.

00:01:58.575 --> 00:01:59.644
Blaaahh!

00:01:59.644 --> 00:02:01.079
It's bad, it's not pretty.

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:02.755
The rest is not much
prettier, but at least

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.835
we got that over with.

00:02:03.835 --> 00:02:06.398
Next, modesty goes out the window!

00:02:06.398 --> 00:02:08.818
When you are giving
birth, you are basically

00:02:08.818 --> 00:02:12.442
a live vagina exhibit
because it's just a cycle

00:02:12.442 --> 00:02:14.406
of people coming in and out of the room,

00:02:14.406 --> 00:02:16.254
checking on your lady parts.

00:02:16.254 --> 00:02:18.176
There's a woman who
will come in every hour

00:02:18.176 --> 00:02:22.141
to shove her hand up and
tell you how far open it is.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:22.974
Okay.

00:02:22.974 --> 00:02:25.605
There'll be a random man
walking in, like lift up

00:02:25.605 --> 00:02:29.435
my hospital gown and be
like, "Mmm, hmm yeah."

00:02:29.435 --> 00:02:30.902
Write something down and leave.

00:02:30.902 --> 00:02:33.069
And I'm like, "Can you at
least tell me your name

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:34.520
"if you're going to be looking at that?!"

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:37.158
But the worst part is you
don't even care at that point.

00:02:37.158 --> 00:02:39.984
I was like, "You can look
as long as looking is gonna

00:02:39.984 --> 00:02:41.392
"help me get this out".

00:02:41.392 --> 00:02:43.158
Next, the flood gates.

00:02:43.158 --> 00:02:45.951
Your water does not
break like in the movies.

00:02:45.951 --> 00:02:48.454
A lot of the time you
will go into labor first

00:02:48.454 --> 00:02:50.233
and then your water will break at the most

00:02:50.233 --> 00:02:51.583
inconvenient time.

00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:54.422
So, in my first labor my
water decided to break

00:02:54.422 --> 00:02:57.719
as the anesthesiologist was
sticking in the epidural

00:02:57.719 --> 00:03:00.580
needle and that's like the most key part,

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.652
because if he misses
with that needle he could

00:03:03.652 --> 00:03:05.807
potentially cripple me or kill me!

00:03:05.807 --> 00:03:09.047
And so he's there just like
"Okay, hold perfectly still,"

00:03:09.047 --> 00:03:10.787
and my body is just like (water splashing)

00:03:10.787 --> 00:03:11.620
"There you go!"

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.996
And then with the second, my water broke

00:03:13.996 --> 00:03:17.401
as the nurse was hunched
over me, checking because

00:03:17.401 --> 00:03:21.256
I wasn't progressing and she
wanted to get a closer look.

00:03:21.256 --> 00:03:24.379
Just like (water splashing)
like blasted her in the chest.

00:03:24.379 --> 00:03:26.593
She was like, "Ohhh!

00:03:26.593 --> 00:03:29.578
And like the water's
crashing around the bed

00:03:29.578 --> 00:03:32.514
and she wrote on her chart copious fluids,

00:03:32.514 --> 00:03:35.465
because she said that was
the most she's ever seen

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:36.693
in her life.

00:03:36.693 --> 00:03:37.530
I'm sorry Linda.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:39.443
I blasted you with amniotic fluid.

00:03:39.443 --> 00:03:42.000
I'm, this one's for you.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.141
So speaking of epidurals,
the epidural is like

00:03:45.141 --> 00:03:48.181
medically sanctioned hard-core drugs.

00:03:48.181 --> 00:03:50.870
And I don't do drugs, but
whatever's in epidurals,

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.558
I'm sure they sell that on the street,

00:03:52.558 --> 00:03:56.495
'cause I was tripping
balls on my epidural.

00:03:56.495 --> 00:03:59.378
With both of the epidurals
I've collectively said

00:03:59.378 --> 00:04:01.734
some of the most embarrassing
things that I've ever said

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:03.254
in my entire life.

00:04:03.254 --> 00:04:05.859
I was telling the nurse about my love

00:04:05.859 --> 00:04:08.094
for Rick Springfield's butt.

00:04:08.094 --> 00:04:11.268
I was telling the anesthesiologist,
in front of my husband,

00:04:11.268 --> 00:04:12.501
how much I loved him.

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:15.243
"Oh my god, I love you so much!

00:04:15.243 --> 00:04:16.684
"You wanna just get married?

00:04:16.684 --> 00:04:18.315
"I just love you so much!"

00:04:18.315 --> 00:04:20.605
It's like waking up the
next morning after being

00:04:20.605 --> 00:04:23.155
totally wasted, and texting
something really embarrassing

00:04:23.155 --> 00:04:24.035
to your ex.

00:04:24.035 --> 00:04:25.924
You like wake up from the epidural

00:04:25.924 --> 00:04:28.529
and you're like, "Oh
god, what did I say?!"

00:04:28.529 --> 00:04:29.780
(groans)

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.462
And I'm very grateful, but
I will never be able to look

00:04:32.462 --> 00:04:34.694
any of those people in the eye again.

00:04:34.694 --> 00:04:37.615
I didn't even know I
liked Rick Springfield

00:04:37.615 --> 00:04:39.917
until I had my second son.

00:04:39.917 --> 00:04:41.760
(teeth clink on wine glass)

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.132
Ow!

00:04:43.132 --> 00:04:47.146
Which brings us to the last
topic, the fear factor.

00:04:47.146 --> 00:04:49.336
Childbirth is probably the most terrifying

00:04:49.336 --> 00:04:51.268
thing I've ever experienced in my life.

00:04:51.268 --> 00:04:55.147
Because you go in to this
completely unknown territory,

00:04:55.147 --> 00:04:57.681
with a plan, you have your birth plan,

00:04:57.681 --> 00:05:00.341
but once you're in the
trenches of childbirth,

00:05:00.341 --> 00:05:03.380
your birth plan is not
necessarily what's gonna work

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:04.916
to get the child out.

00:05:04.916 --> 00:05:07.453
For example, with my youngest

00:05:07.453 --> 00:05:09.838
his heart rate completely dropped

00:05:09.838 --> 00:05:11.414
as I was pushing him out.

00:05:11.414 --> 00:05:13.924
I had no idea what was going
on, it was just all of a

00:05:13.924 --> 00:05:16.618
sudden just pure chaos
and a million people

00:05:16.618 --> 00:05:17.984
rushed into the room.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:20.322
The doctor pulled out a
suction thing, just sucked

00:05:20.322 --> 00:05:22.849
him out of me and handed him
off to some other people.

00:05:22.849 --> 00:05:24.458
I didn't even hear him cry.

00:05:24.458 --> 00:05:26.321
My husband didn't get to cut the cord.

00:05:26.321 --> 00:05:29.635
And my first words, when he
came out, were, "Is he dead?"

00:05:29.635 --> 00:05:31.842
Because I thought that he had died.

00:05:31.842 --> 00:05:34.148
Luckily he did not, but
it's the most terrifying

00:05:34.148 --> 00:05:35.012
thing of all time.

00:05:35.012 --> 00:05:36.659
I'm not trying to scare you.

00:05:36.659 --> 00:05:40.546
I just think that everybody
should go in knowing exactly

00:05:40.546 --> 00:05:42.191
how scary it is.

00:05:42.191 --> 00:05:44.740
And my hope is that by
telling you that it's going

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:48.543
to be scary, that makes
it a little less scary.

00:05:48.543 --> 00:05:50.299
Every mom who has birthed their child

00:05:50.299 --> 00:05:53.371
has gone through this
and you're gonna be okay.

00:05:53.371 --> 00:05:54.287
You're gonna do great.

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:56.391
On a brighter note, once
you have the baby out,

00:05:56.391 --> 00:05:59.308
that's when the really
scary and awful part starts.

00:05:59.308 --> 00:06:00.612
Because you have a kid.

00:06:00.612 --> 00:06:03.440
You think childbirth is
gross, try raising a kid.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:06.363
You think childbirth is
scary, try raising a kid.

00:06:06.363 --> 00:06:07.196
But I'm just kidding.

00:06:07.196 --> 00:06:09.340
They're actually, they're
blessings, it's beautiful,

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:12.315
it's wonderful, kids are just blessings.

00:06:12.315 --> 00:06:14.070
It's like 50% of the time.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.287
So, that's all I've got for today.

00:06:15.287 --> 00:06:17.347
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom

00:06:17.347 --> 00:06:19.799
and if you have a birth story
that you would like to share,

00:06:19.799 --> 00:06:21.954
I would love to read it,
so leave it in the comments

00:06:21.954 --> 00:06:24.517
because I love hearing about
other women's birth stories

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.379
and just all the different
crazy, funny stuff

00:06:26.379 --> 00:06:27.406
that happens.

00:06:27.406 --> 00:06:29.527
I don't know about you,
but this video has made

00:06:29.527 --> 00:06:30.966
me super, super hungry.

00:06:30.966 --> 00:06:32.746
So I'm gonna go eat some pizza.

00:06:32.746 --> 00:06:36.758
Hope you are inspired to have more babies.

00:06:36.758 --> 00:06:38.008
'Til next time!

00:06:41.962 --> 00:06:43.795
Bye, bye, go, go away.

00:06:45.388 --> 00:06:47.437
(giggles)

